WEBVTT

00:00:58.946 --> 00:01:00.335
in order to make it valuable.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.286
I know this because I was asked

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.556
just a year into my career
at Virgin Atlantic

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.656
to be the first ever reverse mentor

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.786
to mentor CEO Craig Kreeger.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.016
I'd met Craig a few times

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.656
and presented to him in meetings,

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.026
but this, it was a whole
different ball game.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.180
Craig had revealed
that he had no black women

00:01:16.204 --> 00:01:17.378
in his inner circle

00:01:17.402 --> 00:01:19.489
and he was keen
to understand my perspective

00:01:19.513 --> 00:01:22.335
on how to build a more inclusive
culture at Virgin Atlantic.

00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:23.565
No pressure.

00:01:23.589 --> 00:01:24.787
Here's what I learned

00:01:24.811 --> 00:01:26.803
about how to make reverse mentoring work.

00:01:26.827 --> 00:01:28.842
Lesson one, make your match thoughtfully.

00:01:28.866 --> 00:01:30.255
Find someone who has a pulse